From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] source: let idle sources wait instead of polling

Every source device runs a thread that polls its device and then sleeps
out the rest of POLL_RATE (2.5 ms), with or without input: ~400 wakeups
a second per source. On the AYANEO Pocket VERT (an evdev gamepad, an
evdev keyboard and the AYANEO haptics hidraw) InputPlumber was 4.8% of
a core and 1555 runs a second at idle, and its threads waking each
other were most of the system's ~1000 function-call IPIs a second.

Let a source say how it may wait once idle (SourceInputDevice::idle_wait):
evdev gamepads, keyboards and touchscreens on their descriptor, which
becomes readable with input and which poll() drains; the AYANEO haptics
source, which only takes commands, on nothing while no rumble is
scheduled. After a second without input or commands such a source
sleeps for up to 20 ms instead: input still wakes it at once, commands
(rumble, LEDs) wait at most 20 ms, and the first event or command puts
it back on POLL_RATE. Every other source polls as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
